Import the C object errno as integer from the header "errno.h".
Import the C constant ERANGE as integer from the header "errno.h".
Import the C constant EDOM as integer from the header "errno.h".
Import the C function strtol taking a pointer to character and a pointer to pointer to character and an integer, returning a long integer, from the header "stdlib.h".
Import the C function sqrt taking a decimal, returning a decimal, from the header "math.h".
Set errno to 0.
Declare big as long integer with value Call strtol with "99999999999999999999999", null pointer, 10 done.
Say errno is equal to ERANGE.
Set errno to 0.
Declare root as decimal with value Call sqrt with 0 minus 1 done.
Say errno is equal to EDOM.
Set errno to 0.
Say errno.
